{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For you went up</b> — when <b>you went up onto my father's bed,</b> immediately <b>you defiled my couch — עלה.</b> From that day when you defiled my couch, my couch was removed, for from that day onward Jacob did not lie with Bilhah. <b>עלה</b> — was removed, like ״אל תעלני בחצי ימי״ (do not bring me up in the middle of my days). Another interpretation: <b>חללת</b> — you defiled that which went up onto my couch, namely you yourself, for at that time you descended from your holiness and became profane, and the birthright and the kingship were lost from you; and so it says: ״ובחללו יצועי אביו נתנה בכורתו ליוסף״ (and when he defiled his father's couch, his birthright was given to Joseph). <b>יצועי עלה</b> — one may say that he said this to the tribes, meaning: do not wonder if I speak harshly to him, for he sinned greatly, for he went up onto my couch."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:09.170947922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}